    "author_type": "agent",
    "content": "[@Dev A](mention://agent/e1ec8660-8c64-43a2-bdbe-c582b5d1d23c) Implementation is ready for your review.\n\n**Root cause**\n\n`_get_search_url()` tested `term in url.searchengines` even when `_parse_search_term()` had already consumed a leading engine name. I now preserve whether an explicit engine prefix was present and honor `url.open_base_url` only when it was not, so only a completely bare engine name opens its base URL.\n\n**Diff**\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/qutebrowser/utils/urlutils.py b/qutebrowser/utils/urlutils.py\nindex 5b5d93301..0ab56c9d2 100644\n--- a/qutebrowser/utils/urlutils.py\n+++ b/qutebrowser/utils/urlutils.py\n@@ -110,13 +110,15 @@ def _get_search_url(txt: str) -\u003e QUrl:\n     log.url.debug(\"Finding search engine for {!r}\".format(txt))\n     engine, term = _parse_search_term(txt)\n     assert term\n+    has_engine = engine is not None\n     if engine is None:\n         engine = 'DEFAULT'\n     template = config.val.url.searchengines[engine]\n     quoted_term = urllib.parse.quote(term, safe='')\n     url = qurl_from_user_input(template.format(quoted_term))\n \n-    if config.val.url.open_base_url and term in config.val.url.searchengines:\n+    if (config.val.url.open_base_url and not has_engine and\n+            term in config.val.url.searchengines):\n         url = qurl_from_user_input(config.val.url.searchengines[term])\n         url.setPath(None)  # type: ignore\n         url.setFragment(None)  # type: ignore\ndiff --git a/tests/unit/utils/test_urlutils.py b/tests/unit/utils/test_urlutils.py\nindex 060ccfc84..9bb879920 100644\n--- a/tests/unit/utils/test_urlutils.py\n+++ b/tests/unit/utils/test_urlutils.py\n@@ -285,6 +285,9 @@ def test_special_urls(url, special):\n     ('test testfoo', 'www.qutebrowser.org', 'q=testfoo'),\n     ('test testfoo bar foo', 'www.qutebrowser.org', 'q=testfoo bar foo'),\n     ('test testfoo ', 'www.qutebrowser.org', 'q=testfoo'),\n+    ('test path-search', 'www.qutebrowser.org', 'q=path-search'),\n+    ('test path-search bar/baz', 'www.qutebrowser.org',\n+     'q=path-search bar%2Fbaz'),\n     ('!python testfoo', 'www.example.com', 'q=%21python testfoo'),\n     ('blub testfoo', 'www.example.com', 'q=blub testfoo'),\n     ('stripped ', 'www.example.com', 'q=stripped'),\n```\n\n**Test output**\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/utils/test_urlutils.py` → `245 passed, 1 skipped in 2.12s`\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/utils/` → `21 failed, 1004 passed, 43 skipped, 2 xfailed in 14.92s`\n- Baseline `a55f4db26b4b1caa304dd4b842a4103445fdccc7`, same full command → `21 failed, 1000 passed, 43 skipped, 2 xfailed in 10.98s`\n\nThe full-suite failures are the same 21 pre-existing failures on the untouched base commit; the patch adds four passing parameterized cases. Please review this diff. After your approval, I’ll attach the single `final.patch` and move the issue to In Review.",
