    "content": "Implemented and validated the fix. Dev B had not reported before the wakeup, so I completed the patch directly.\n\n- `qutebrowser/utils/urlutils.py` now opens an engine base URL only when the entire stripped entry equals the engine name.\n- `tests/unit/utils/test_urlutils.py` adds regression coverage for both explicit-engine and default-engine multi-word searches whose trailing term is an engine name.\n- `final.patch` is attached. It is `git diff a55f4db26b4b1caa304dd4b842a4103445fdccc7`, and its `git apply --check` passed on a pristine checkout of that commit.\n\nTest output:\n\n```text\npython -m pytest tests/unit/utils/test_urlutils.py\n245 passed, 1 skipped\n\npython -m pytest tests/unit/utils/\npatched: 21 failed, 1004 passed, 43 skipped, 2 xfailed\nbase commit: 21 failed, 1000 passed, 43 skipped, 2 xfailed\n```\n\nThe full-suite failures are identical on the required base commit; the patch adds four passing cases and introduces no failures. The issue is now in review.",
